> Thanks @azamikram! I assume the test results were all with the python frontend. Would you be able to also see how it compares with the rust frontend (`VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1`)?

@njhill, I just realized that testing with rust frontend would mean implementing the changes in the rust frontend (I was hoping that somehow I would be able to reuse the python ZMQ implementation but [rust frontend maintains its own scheduler stats](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/rust/src/engine-core-client/src/metrics.rs#L158)).

Given the scope, I think it would be better to split these in two separate PRs? This one only focuses on python frontend and then I can open another one with the support and results for the rust frontend. Let me know what you think.

